WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
Everything on an estimate.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.567
Open an estimate. Click a row to open the estimate. The tour opens this one.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:18.400
Back to the customer. The customer's name above the title opens their page: phones, notes, and all their estimates, jobs and invoices.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:29.633
Where it stands. The number and status sit above the title. Here: the status (Draft, Sent, Won, Lost), any follow-up due, the address, phone and when it was sent.

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:35.300
Customer view. Switch to see the estimate exactly as the customer gets it.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:48.500
The real document. The saved copy the customer receives by email, as a PDF or on paper: sections, totals, add-ons and terms. Print / PDF is just above it.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.533
Back to Build. Build is where you write the estimate.

00:00:53.033 --> 00:01:02.600
Save. Saves sections, prices and details. "Unsaved changes" shows beside it until you do. ⌘S or Ctrl+S saves too.

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:15.500
Send. Opens the send choices: email the online link (best), email it, print or save as PDF, or "I sent it another way". Each marks it Sent and starts the follow-ups.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:26.067
Won. When the customer says yes. One step makes the contract, the payment schedule and the job. The tour "Mark an estimate won or lost" shows it.

00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:35.600
Lost. When they say no: pick why (price, someone else, timing…). It stays for the close-rate report, and Reopen brings it back as a draft.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:47.000
Measure. Opens a satellite photo of the property. Trace the patio, driveway, beds or wall line; back here a Measured card turns each area into a section.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:56.100
Duplicate. Copies this estimate as a new draft for the same customer, e.g. a second option, and opens the copy.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:07.067
Sections. Each section is one line the customer sees (Patio, Walls, Lighting…) with its own total. The labor price and the materials go inside it.

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:16.367
Taxable or Tax exempt. One click switches the section between Taxable and Tax exempt; the sales tax in Totals follows.

00:02:16.867 --> 00:02:28.233
Materials, hidden or shown. The materials in a section. Unticked lines are hidden: the customer sees only the section total. Cost and price give you the margin.

00:02:28.733 --> 00:02:37.667
Optional add-ons. A dashed section is an optional add-on: priced on its own and left out of the total until the customer takes it.

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:48.933
Add a section. Search the catalogue: a service brings its price, unit, crew-hours, tax setting and its kit of materials. Blank section starts an empty one.

00:02:49.433 --> 00:02:57.967
Totals. Subtotal, sales tax at this estimate's rate and the total. Optional add-ons are shown apart, not in the total.

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:09.033
Customer copy. Open the customer copy shows the document full width; Print / PDF prints it or saves a PDF you can attach to your own email.

00:03:09.533 --> 00:03:20.000
Contract terms. The payment schedule the contract gets, what each payment comes to, and the NJ ST-8 capital improvement switch (no sales tax).

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:32.300
Online estimate. The customer's link: Sent, Opened, Signed. They tick add-ons, initial the terms and sign; signing makes the job, contract and deposit invoice.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:42.500
Follow-ups. What the automatic follow-up does next and when, with an on / off switch for this estimate. Emails and texts about it are listed here.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:53.167
Margin. Materials at cost plus crew-hours at your labor cost: cost, gross profit, margin % and crew-hours. Never shown to the customer.

00:03:53.633 --> 00:04:04.467
Material selections. What the customer picked at the supplier: pavers, wall block, caps, steps… It goes on the selection sheet, the proposal and the work order.

00:04:04.967 --> 00:04:15.933
Details. Title, salesperson, valid until, tax %, a message to the customer, an office note they never see, and terms. Save keeps your changes.

00:04:16.433 --> 00:04:22.033
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
